    "Narrative": "<p>On-call referral received on Thursday, March 25th, 2021 for CJAMS input:</p><p><br></p><p>3/24/21 @ 8:15pm</p><p>RS: Sgt Kalinsky – Cecil County Sherriff’s Office – 410-996-5511</p><p>Mother: Diana Rolfe (12/15/88)</p><p>2 Vanessa Ave, Rising Sun, MD</p><p>Other adult: Robert DiSabatino</p><p>Child: Genesis Keyes (DOB: 12/25/2014)</p><p><br></p><p>On 3/24/21, RS contacted CCDSS to report the following:</p><p><br></p><p>RS reported Deputies were currently at Ms. Rolfe’s residence, after being dispatched for an overdose. RS reported Ms. Rolfe had overdosed and required 2 doses of Narcan, in order to be awakened. RS reported Ms. Rolfe’s boyfriend was present and called 911. RS reported Ms. Rolfe’s daughter was present at the time of the overdose. RS reported Ms. Rolfe refused transport to the hospital. RS reported Ms. Rolfe’s boyfriend resides in the residence and was available for supervision of Genesis.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>No information was offered regarding domestic violence, mental health, parental capabilities, or substance abuse pertaining to the boyfriend.  No Police Report has been submitted at this time.  This referral is being screened in as a neglect investigation.</p><p><br></p><p>This referral was not screened within two hours as it was received on-call.</p><p><br></p>",
